  "notes": "West leads the ♠K against 5♥. South wins West's spade opening lead with the ♠A. South has a possible trump loser and at least 1 loser in clubs, depending on the location of the ♣A. Dummy's diamond suit will provide ample discards for all of South's spade and club losers once trumps are drawn.\n\nSouth may have to lose a heart trick. South doesn't mind losing this trick to East as East will not be able to attack the ♣K effectively. If West should gain the lead in hearts, however, the contract will be in danger if East has the ♣A.\n\nSouth can virtually guarantee his contract by passing the ♥J (or any other of South's small hearts) through West at trick 2. If South wins the trick the remaining trumps can be drawn, finessing again if East discards on the first round.\n\nIf East can win the ♥Q, the contract is safe. Whether or not the defense cashes the ♣A, South can easily draw trump and take the rest of the tricks.",
  "commentary_paragraphs": [
    "West leads the ♠K against 5♥. South wins West's spade opening lead with the ♠A. South has a possible trump loser and at least 1 loser in clubs, depending on the location of the ♣A. Dummy's diamond suit will provide ample discards for all of South's spade and club losers once trumps are drawn.",
    "South may have to lose a heart trick. South doesn't mind losing this trick to East as East will not be able to attack the ♣K effectively. If West should gain the lead in hearts, however, the contract will be in danger if East has the ♣A.",
    "South can virtually guarantee his contract by passing the ♥J (or any other of South's small hearts) through West at trick 2. If South wins the trick the remaining trumps can be drawn, finessing again if East discards on the first round.",
    "If East can win the ♥Q, the contract is safe. Whether or not the defense cashes the ♣A, South can easily draw trump and take the rest of the tricks."
